# css-scope-inline

16-line zero-dep JS. `<style>` inside any element → `me`/`this`/`self` selectors scope to parent. No class names needed.

Repo: https://github.com/gnat/css-scope-inline
Demo: https://gnat.github.io/css-scope-inline/example.html

## Install

```html
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/gnat/css-scope-inline@main/script.js"></script>
```

Or self-host `script.js`, or inline 16-line snippet in `<head>`. No build/npm/config.

## Core

```html
<div>
    <style>
        me { background: red; }           /* styles THIS div */
        me button { background: blue; }   /* buttons INSIDE this div */
        me:hover { opacity: 0.8; }        /* pseudo-classes work */
    </style>
    <button>I'm blue</button>
</div>
```

MutationObserver watches DOM. On `<style>` detect:
1. Generate unique class `.me__1234`
2. Add class to `<style>` parent
3. Replace `me`/`this`/`self` with `.me__1234`
4. Mark `<style ready>` — skip on re-scan

Fully scoped, no flash, works with dynamic DOM (htmx swaps, ajax).

## Selector Keywords

`me`, `this`, `self` — interchangeable. Pick what reads best.

## Responsive Shorthand

Script rewrites short media queries:

**Mobile-first (min-width):** `sm`=640 `md`=768 `lg`=1024 `xl`=1280 `xx`=1536

**Desktop-first (max-width):** `xs-`=639 `sm-`=767 `md-`=1023 `lg-`=1279 `xl-`=1535

`xx` not `2xl` — avoids breaking CSS highlighters.

```html
<div>
    <style>
        me { font-size: 14px; }
        @media md { me { font-size: 18px; } }
        @media lg { me { font-size: 22px; } }
    </style>
    Responsive text
</div>
```

## CSS Nesting

Native nesting works:

```html
<div>
    <style>
        me {
            background: #eee;
            & button {
                color: blue;
                &:hover { color: darkblue; }
            }
        }
    </style>
    <button>Nested styles work!</button>
</div>
```

## Scoped @keyframes

Script auto-strips `.me__` from animation names:

```html
<style>
    @keyframes slide { from { opacity:0 } to { opacity:1 } }
    me { animation: slide 1s ease; }
</style>
```

Or explicit: `@keyframes me__slide` — both work.

## Positional Selectors

Attribute shorthand beats `nth-child`:

```html
<div>
    <style>
        me [n1] { background: yellow; }
        me [n2] { background: green; }
    </style>
    <div n1>First</div>
    <div n2>Second</div>
</div>
```

## Inline ↔ External CSS

Replace `me` with real class/selector to move to `.css` file. Reverse to bring back inline.

## Works With

- **htmx** — MutationObserver re-runs on DOM swap. Scoped styles auto-apply to dynamic content.
- **Surreal** — Companion lib, scopes `<script>` same way. https://github.com/gnat/surreal
- **Any vanilla HTML** — No framework needed.

## Patterns

### Card w/ hover

```html
<div class="card">
    <style>
        me { padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); }
        me:hover { box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.2); transition: box-shadow 0.2s; }
        me h2 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.2rem; }
        me p { color: #666; }
    </style>
    <h2>Title</h2>
    <p>Description text</p>
</div>
```

### Nav w/ CSS vars

```html
<style>
    :root { --nav-bg: #1a1a2e; --nav-active: #e94560; }
</style>
<nav>
    <style>
        me { background: var(--nav-bg); padding: 0.5rem 1rem; display: flex; gap: 1rem; }
        me a { color: white; text-decoration: none; padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem; border-radius: 4px; }
        me a:hover, me a.active { background: var(--nav-active); }
    </style>
    <a href="/" class="active">Home</a>
    <a href="/about">About</a>
</nav>
```

### Responsive grid

```html
<div>
    <style>
        me { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
        @media md { me { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
        @media lg { me { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
    </style>
    <div>Item 1</div>
    <div>Item 2</div>
    <div>Item 3</div>
</div>
```

## Full Script (16 lines)

```js
// 🌘 CSS Scope Inline (https://github.com/gnat/css-scope-inline)
window.cssScopeCount ??= 1
window.cssScope ??= new MutationObserver(mutations => {
    document?.body?.querySelectorAll('style:not([ready])').forEach(node => {
        var scope = 'me__'+(window.cssScopeCount++)
        node.parentNode.classList.add(scope)
        node.textContent = node.textContent
        .replace(/(?:^|\.|(\s|[^a-zA-Z0-9\-\_]))(me|this|self)(?![a-zA-Z])/g, '$1.'+scope)
        .replace(/((@keyframes|animation:|animation-name:)[^{};]*)\.me__/g, '$1me__')
        .replace(/(?:@media)\s(xs-|sm-|md-|lg-|xl-|sm|md|lg|xl|xx)/g,
            (match, part1) => { return '@media '+({'sm':'(min-width: 640px)','md':'(min-width: 768px)',
            'lg':'(min-width: 1024px)','xl':'(min-width: 1280px)','xx':'(min-width: 1536px)',
            'xs-':'(max-width: 639px)','sm-':'(max-width: 767px)','md-':'(max-width: 1023px)',
            'lg-':'(max-width: 1279px)','xl-':'(max-width: 1535px)'}[part1]) }
        )
        node.setAttribute('ready', '')
    })
}).observe(document.documentElement, {childList: true, subtree: true})
```

## Gotchas

- **Requires JS** — MutationObserver applies styles, not parser.
- **`me` needs non-letter after** — `me {}` works, `menu {}` untouched (correct).
- **Multi-include safe** — shared globals, one observer runs.
- **No `me`/`this`/`self` in `<style>`** — left untouched. Safe to mix scoped + global.
- **`ready` attr** = processed marker. Never manually add to unprocessed `<style>`.

</css-scope-inline>
