---
name: microvm-nix
description: Use when working with microvm.nix — the Nix Flake for running lightweight NixOS MicroVMs. Triggers on microvm.nix, NixOS MicroVMs, qemu/cloud-hypervisor/firecracker/crosvm/kvmtool/stratovirt/alioth/vfkit hypervisor in Nix, `microvm.vms`/`microvm.host`/`microvm.shares`/`microvm.interfaces` options, virtiofs/9p `/nix/store` sharing into VMs, TAP+bridge VM networking, `/var/lib/microvms`, `microvm` CLI, declarative or imperative MicroVM deployment, NixOS replacement for Docker/LXC/systemd-nspawn with stronger isolation, vfkit on macOS via Apple Virtualization.framework.
---

# microvm.nix

Flake for declarative, lightweight NixOS VMs. Stronger isolation than containers (own kernel), smaller closure than full NixOS images (read-only erofs/squashfs root + shared host `/nix/store`).

Docs: https://microvm-nix.github.io/microvm.nix
Repo: https://github.com/microvm-nix/microvm.nix

## Hypervisors

| Hypervisor | Notes |
|---|---|
| `qemu` | Default. Most features. |
| `cloud-hypervisor` | Rust. Fast boot. |
| `firecracker` | Rust. AWS Lambda-style. |
| `crosvm` | Rust. ChromeOS. |
| `kvmtool` | Lightweight C. |
| `stratovirt` | Rust. |
| `alioth` | Rust. |
| `vfkit` | macOS only. Apple Virtualization.framework. **No 9p — use virtiofs.** |

Set: `microvm.hypervisor = "cloud-hypervisor";`

## Host module

```nix
imports = [ inputs.microvm.nixosModules.host ];
microvm.autostart = [ "vm1" "vm2" ];
```

Provides:
- `/var/lib/microvms/<name>/` — VM state dir
- systemd services: `microvm@<name>.service`, tap setup, virtiofsd
- `microvm` CLI tool

## Guest module options

```nix
imports = [ inputs.microvm.nixosModules.microvm ];
microvm = {
  hypervisor = "qemu";          # default qemu
  vcpu = 2;                     # default 1
  mem = 1024;                   # default 512 MB
  hotplugMem = 2048;            # virtio-mem max additional
  storeOnDisk = false;          # true = compressed store disk; false = share host store
  writableStoreOverlay = "/nix/.rw-store";  # optional rw overlay (needs volume, not share)

  shares = [ ... ];             # virtiofs / 9p mounts
  volumes = [ ... ];            # disk images, auto-created/formatted
  interfaces = [ ... ];         # network
  forwardPorts = [ ... ];       # IPv4 only, qemu user-net
  vsock.cid = 42;               # AF_VSOCK
  devices = [ ... ];            # PCI/USB passthrough
};
```

## Shares — 9p vs virtiofs

| | 9p | virtiofs |
|---|---|---|
| Daemon | None (built into hv) | `virtiofsd` (auto via host module; vfkit built-in) |
| Speed | Slow | Fast |
| vfkit | ❌ | ✅ |
| Default | yes | — |

```nix
microvm.shares = [
  { proto = "virtiofs"; tag = "ro-store"; source = "/nix/store"; mountPoint = "/nix/.ro-store"; }
  { proto = "virtiofs"; tag = "home";     source = "/srv/vm1/home"; mountPoint = "/home"; }
];
```

**Always share host `/nix/store`** — avoids building huge image per VM.

**ZFS source**: dataset must have `xattr=sa acltype=posixacl`.

**Writable overlay**: must use `microvm.volumes`, not shares (Linux overlayfs limitation on virtiofs/9p lower dirs is fine but upperdir cannot be on them).

## Networking — TAP + bridge

```nix
# guest
microvm.interfaces = [{
  type = "tap";
  id   = "vm-test1";          # name pattern matched on host
  mac  = "02:00:00:00:00:01"; # locally-administered prefix 02:
}];

# host (systemd-networkd)
systemd.network.networks."10-lan" = {
  matchConfig.Name = [ "eno1" "vm-*" ];
  networkConfig.Bridge = "br0";
};
systemd.network.netdevs."br0" = { netdevConfig = { Kind = "bridge"; Name = "br0"; }; };
```

Interface types: `user` (qemu slirp, NAT), `tap`, `macvtap`, `bridge`.

Watch out: `systemd-networkd` will also try to manage Docker `veth*` inside guest — exclude via `matchConfig` if running Docker in MicroVM.

## Declarative VMs (host config defines guest)

```nix
microvm.vms.vm1 = {
  inherit (inputs) nixpkgs;            # or pkgs = ...
  config = { ... }: {
    networking.hostName = "vm1";
    microvm.hypervisor = "cloud-hypervisor";
    microvm.shares = [ /* share /nix/store */ ];
    microvm.interfaces = [ /* tap */ ];
  };
};

# Or reference external flake:
microvm.vms.vm2 = {
  flake = inputs.myvm;
  updateFlake = "github:me/myvm";   # for `microvm -u vm2`
};
```

## Imperative CLI

`microvm` tool (installed by host module). Subcommands include create/list/update/start/run — exact flags vary by version (online docs imperative page 404'd at time of writing). Run `microvm --help`.

Common flow:
- `microvm -c <name>` — create from declarative config
- `microvm -u <name>` — update (re-deploy after flake change)
- `microvm -l` — list
- `microvm -R <name>` — run in foreground (debug)
- `systemctl start microvm@<name>` — start as service

## Minimal flake skeleton

```nix
{
  inputs.nixpkgs.url      = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-unstable";
  inputs.microvm.url      = "github:microvm-nix/microvm.nix";
  inputs.microvm.inputs.nixpkgs.follows = "nixpkgs";

  outputs = { self, nixpkgs, microvm }: {
    nixosConfigurations.host = nixpkgs.lib.nixosSystem {
      system = "x86_64-linux";
      modules = [
        microvm.nixosModules.host
        ({ ... }: {
          microvm.autostart = [ "vm1" ];
          microvm.vms.vm1.config = { ... }: {
            networking.hostName = "vm1";
            users.users.root.password = "";
            services.openssh.enable = true;
            microvm.hypervisor = "cloud-hypervisor";
            microvm.mem = 1024;
            microvm.interfaces = [{
              type = "tap"; id = "vm-vm1"; mac = "02:00:00:00:00:01";
            }];
            microvm.shares = [{
              proto = "virtiofs"; tag = "ro-store";
              source = "/nix/store"; mountPoint = "/nix/.ro-store";
            }];
          };
        })
      ];
    };
  };
}
```

## Gotchas

- vfkit (macOS): no 9p — virtiofs only.
- Writable `/nix/store` overlay: must use volume; cannot live on share.
- Forgetting to share `/nix/store` → multi-GB stage1 squashfs per VM.
- `forwardPorts` IPv4 only, qemu user-net only.
- TAP names should match host `vm-*` networkd rule, else no bridge attach.
- MAC: use `02:` locally-administered prefix to avoid collisions.
- Defaults: 1 vCPU, 512 MB RAM — bump for real workloads.
- `microvm.autostart` only takes effect after `microvm -c` has staged the VM in `/var/lib/microvms`.

## Doc subpages

- `intro.html` — quickstart
- `declarative.html` — `microvm.vms` on host
- `host.html` — host module
- `microvm-options.html` — full option reference
